    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d55">

                <pb facs="0235" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg119"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">555.H1/13</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Italian Embassy to the
                            Department of State</hi><anchor n="82"
                        xml:id="d55-f1"/></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        type="received-date" when="1923-10-18">undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide Memoire</hi></p>
                <p>The International Conference for emigration and immigration to be held in Rome
                    during the first months of 1924 is assuming <pb facs="0236" n="120"
                        xml:id="pg120"/> considerable importance on account of the large number of
                    States that have accepted to participate.</p>
                <p>In consideration of this it would perhaps be advisable to have a preliminary
                    meeting of the experts of the Countries most interested in view of determining
                    the technical questions to be discussed by the several sections of the
                    Conference in Rome.</p>
                <p>The meeting could take place in December or January in Genoa, Pallanza, Geneva or
                    Ouchy.</p>
                <p>The Italian Government would like to know if such a proposal would be agreeable
                    to the Government of the United States and which date and locality would be
                    considered most convenient.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
